.TH CEC-MUSICCAST-BRIDGE 1 "October 2026" "0.2.0"
.SH NAME
cec-musiccast-bridge \- control Yamaha MusicCast using HDMI-CEC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cec-musiccast-bridge
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Presents an audio system on the HDMI-CEC bus and forwards TV power and
volume commands to a MusicCast receiver. With automatic discovery, the
receiver is selected using SSDP and its Yamaha Extended Control API.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display command line help.
.TP
.B \-\-discover
Print a JSON array of receivers without opening a CEC adapter. Return 1
when none are found. Discovery does not change receiver settings.
.TP
.BI "\-c, \-\-config " file
Read key=value settings. Explicit command line options take precedence.
.TP
.BI "\-a, \-\-address " address
Receiver hostname or IPv4 address, or auto (default) for SSDP discovery.
.TP
.BI "\-\-device-id " id
Select the stable Yamaha device ID. Required when discovery finds more
than one receiver.
.TP
.BI "\-i, \-\-input " input
Receiver input connected to the TV (default: optical1).
.TP
.BI "\-v, \-\-volume " volume
Power-on volume in Yamaha units, not percent (default: 90).
.TP
.BI "\-\-discovery-timeout " seconds
SSDP listening time from 1 to 30 seconds (default: 5). Each candidate
is subsequently probed with an HTTP timeout of 3 seconds.
.TP
.BI "\-\-interface " address
Local IPv4 address for SSDP, or all active multicast interfaces by default.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/cec-musiccast-bridge.conf
.SH SERVICE
The Debian package enables and starts cec-musiccast-bridge.service.
The service retries discovery after startup failures and periodically
reconnects to the same device ID when its address changes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
